---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Penguin-Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../../components/Navbar.astro';

const currentDate = new Date();
let currentYear = currentDate.getFullYear();
---

<Layout title="Penguins">
    <head>
        <meta charset="UTF-8">
        <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
        <title>Gentoo Penguin</title>
    </head>
    <body>
        <header class="header">
            <h1>Gentoo Penguin</h1>
        </header>
        <Navbar/>
        <main>
            <div class="container">
                <nav class="contents">
                    <h2>Contents:</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li><a href="#overview">Overview</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#diet">Diet</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#behavior">Social Behavior</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#facts">Facts</a></li>
                    </ul>
                </nav>

                <section id="overview">
                    <h2>Overview</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Scientific Name: Pygoscelis papua</li>
                        <li>Size: Approximately 76-91 cm (30-36 inches) tall, weighing 4.5-8.5 kg (9.9-18.7 lbs).</li>
                        <li>Habitat: Found on many subantarctic islands and the Antarctic Peninsula. They breed on ice-free areas along the coast.</li>
                        <li>Conservation Status: Near Threatened</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>
                <section id="diet">
                    <h2>Diet</h2>
                    <p>Gentoo Penguins have a varied diet consisting mainly of crustaceans (especially krill), fish, and squid. The proportions can vary depending on location and season.</p>
                </section>
                <section id="behavior">
                    <h2>Social Behavior</h2>
                    <p>Gentoo Penguins live in colonies that can range in size from a few pairs to several thousand. They are known for their relatively gentle and less aggressive nature compared to some other penguin species. They engage in courtship rituals involving pebble carrying and vocalizations to form strong pair bonds that often last for multiple breeding seasons.</p>
                </section>
                <section id="facts">
                    <h2>Interesting Facts</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li>They are easily recognizable by the wide white stripe across the top of their heads.</li>
                        <li>Gentoo Penguins build nests out of stones, and the size of the pebble pile can be part of their courtship display.</li>
                        <li>They are the fastest underwater swimmers among all penguins, reaching speeds of up to 36 km/h (22 mph) in short bursts.</li>
                        <li>Chicks form crèches (groups) for warmth and protection while their parents forage.</li>
                        <li>Their populations are generally stable or even increasing in some areas, but they are still monitored due to potential threats like climate change and fisheries.</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>
            </div>
            <footer>
                <p><span class="copyleft">&copy;</span> PengiCoder & MrPiggy105, { currentYear }</p>
            </footer>
        </main>
    </body>
</Layout>

<style>
    .contents ul {
        list-style-type: none;
        padding: 0;
    }

    .contents li {
        margin-bottom: 10px;
    }

    section {
        overflow: hidden;
        margin-bottom: 20px;
        margin-left: 30%;
    }

    h1{
        text-align: center;
        height: 100%;
        font-family: 'Orkney', Arial;
    }
</style>